CLEAN-ROOM NOTICE

zssim is an independent, clean-room implementation written from scratch in Zig.
It implements image-quality algorithms described in public, peer-reviewed
research literature and open standards (see the citations in README.md). It is
NOT derived from, and contains no source code copied or translated from, any
existing implementation. The algorithms themselves (SSIM, MS-SSIM, CIE L*a*b*,
ICtCp, and the sRGB/PQ/HLG transfer functions) are not copyrightable; only
specific implementations are, and this is an original one.
